1
00:00:00,520 --> 00:00:05,610
Comparing numbers within 1000

2
00:00:10,530 --> 00:00:17,600
Compare two numbers 437 and 515.

3
00:00:22,880 --> 00:00:28,010
Compare the hundreds of the two numbers.

4
00:00:29,100 --> 00:00:32,400
4 < 5

5
00:00:35,950 --> 00:00:41,850
437 < 515

6
00:00:43,930 --> 00:00:49,460
So the number with the larger hundreds is greater.

7
00:00:53,020 --> 00:01:01,520
Compare two numbers 316 and 142.

8
00:01:06,290 --> 00:01:10,990
Compare the hundreds of 2 numbers.

9
00:01:11,770 --> 00:01:15,290
3 > 1

10
00:01:18,510 --> 00:01:24,900
So 316 > 142

11
00:01:26,460 --> 00:01:33,740
142 < 316

12
00:01:35,090 --> 00:01:43,090
Compare two numbers 294 and 236.

13
00:01:47,090 --> 00:01:52,440
Compare the hundreds of the two numbers.

14
00:01:52,840 --> 00:01:56,210
2 = 2

15
00:01:58,030 --> 00:02:01,440
Hundreds are equal

16
00:02:01,620 --> 00:02:08,860
Continue comparing the tens of the two numbers

17
00:02:10,300 --> 00:02:14,560
9 > 3

18
00:02:18,340 --> 00:02:24,100
294 > 236

19
00:02:26,740 --> 00:02:33,390
236 < 294

20
00:02:37,000 --> 00:02:55,620
So first we compare hundreds, if hundreds are equal continue comparing tens, whichever has larger tens is greater.

21
00:02:58,500 --> 00:03:06,990
Compare two numbers 365 and 362.

22
00:03:09,900 --> 00:03:15,980
The hundreds of both numbers are equal to 3

23
00:03:18,250 --> 00:03:24,200
The tens of both numbers are equal to 6

24
00:03:27,130 --> 00:03:34,060
Comparing the ones of both numbers we have:

25
00:03:34,750 --> 00:03:38,640
5 > 2

26
00:03:41,070 --> 00:03:47,860
So 365 > 362

27
00:03:49,860 --> 00:03:56,300
362 < 365

28
00:03:57,440 --> 00:04:04,340
To summarize, to compare two three-digit numbers we do as follows:

29
00:04:05,720 --> 00:04:12,460
First, we compare the hundreds of the two numbers

30
00:04:13,620 --> 00:04:20,450
whichever has larger hundreds is greater

31
00:04:21,480 --> 00:04:25,870
if the hundreds of the two numbers are equal

32
00:04:26,120 --> 00:04:30,530
we continue comparing tens

33
00:04:33,150 --> 00:04:38,280
whichever has larger tens is greater

34
00:04:40,730 --> 00:04:45,010
if hundreds are equal

35
00:04:46,130 --> 00:04:50,350
tens are equal

36
00:04:50,940 --> 00:04:55,120
we continue comparing ones

37
00:04:57,700 --> 00:05:04,660
whichever has larger ones is greater

